-- RUIN Pathfinder routes
-- A route is a list of steps. "accept", "complete" and "turnin" steps name
-- a quest and tick off by themselves; "go" and "note" steps are ticked by
-- hand (or skipped with the > button).
--
-- Quest steps carry the quest ID (qid), so they tick off and find their spot
-- even where a translated client names the quest differently, and RUIN
-- Pathfinder can ask the quest database about them.
--
-- A step may carry a place:  at = { zone = "Elwynn Forest", x = 48.9, y = 41.6 }
-- (map percentages). The tracker's arrow points there while you're in that zone.
--
-- Alliance 1-60 levelling routes are made by RUIN's route planner
-- (tests/tools/plan_routes.lua) from RUIN Quest Data: each picks, level by
-- level, the zone's quests that give the most experience an hour solo, moves
-- from zone to zone the way the game expects, and ends by naming 1-3 routes
-- to start next. Steps carry lv (your level about then) and t (minutes since
-- the route's start), estimates for the time budget. Don't edit these routes
-- by hand: change the planner and run it again.
